# ─── mcode Docker build context ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is a DENY-list on purpose.
#
# The previous version was a whitelist that ended with `!node_modules/**`.
# That copied the Windows host's node_modules — including win32-compiled
# node-pty / cpu-features / ssh2 .node binaries — into a Linux container.
# The binaries could not load, and the backend crashed on boot. The
# Dockerfile now installs dependencies INSIDE the image, so the host tree
# must never enter the context.

# ─── Dependencies (installed in-image, never copied) ──────────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.npm

# ─── Build output (rebuilt in-image) ──────────────────────────────────────────
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── Test / coverage artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage
**/coverage
.nyc_output
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results

# ─── VCS, CI, editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# ─── Local agent scratch + logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.mcode
logs
**/logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Passed at runtime via compose `env_file` / `environment`, never baked in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker.example
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
*.pfx

# ─── Scratch output from local test/debug runs ────────────────────────────────
*.txt
cli2.txt
root-all.txt
vitest-out.txt
web-tests-*.txt
packages/web/*.txt

# ─── Docs (not needed at runtime) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
docs
**/*.md
!README.md
